WEBVTT

00:00:09.120 --> 00:00:10.240
(CLATTERING)

00:00:10.880 --> 00:00:12.640
(CROWD GASPING)

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:20.400
(SIRENS WAILING)

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:33.920
MAN ON RADIO:
(SING-SONG) W-H-L-Z

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:35.560
RADIO HOST: Welcome back
to Piston Cup Talk.

00:00:35.720 --> 00:00:39.400
Around the clock where we do nothing
but talk racing. Let's get to it.

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:40.760
Starting of course

00:00:40.800 --> 00:00:41.800
-with Lightning McQueen.
-(SNORING)

00:00:42.280 --> 00:00:46.120
With the season just two weeks away,
there's still no official announcement.

00:00:46.280 --> 00:00:49.440
But with number 95 coming off
his worst year on record--

00:00:49.600 --> 00:00:52.080
Don't shoot the messenger here, folks.
I think it's safe to assume...

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:55.560
that Lightning McQueen's
racing days are over.

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.880
Meanwhile, Jackson Storm
is looking even faster--

00:00:58.960 --> 00:01:00.200
(TURNS OFF RADIO)

00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:01.960
(SIGHS HEAVILY)

00:01:03.520 --> 00:01:04.960
(WHIRRING)

00:01:05.520 --> 00:01:06.640
COMMENTATOR:
For the checkered flag.

00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:10.120
As they enter the final lap,
the number 6 and number 12 cars...

00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:14.240
are still fighting it out for the lead.
But wait! Here he comes!

00:01:14.440 --> 00:01:17.440
It's the Fabulous Hudson Hornet
knocking at their door.

00:01:17.640 --> 00:01:21.800
What's he got up his sleeve today?
And there it is!

00:01:21.960 --> 00:01:24.760
With one move, he's past them.

00:01:24.800 --> 00:01:26.640
The Hornet takes a decisive lead.

00:01:28.960 --> 00:01:32.760
He's left the pack behind.
His crew chief, Smokey, is loving it!

00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:36.320
It's unbelievable!
Oh, no! He's in trouble!

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:41.600
-The Hudson Hornet has lost control!
-(HUDSON CRASHING)

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:43.560
(CARS GASPING)

00:01:44.480 --> 00:01:46.480
What should have been
a scene of jubilation

00:01:46.560 --> 00:01:49.000
-has turned tragic, folks.
-(SIRENS WAILING)

00:01:49.080 --> 00:01:51.640
As we await news
on the Hudson Hornet's condition.

00:01:51.680 --> 00:01:53.440
After such a devastating crash...

00:01:53.560 --> 00:01:57.000
we can only hope that
this race today wasn't his last.

00:01:58.440 --> 00:01:59.520
(PROJECTOR CLICKS)

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:04.520
HUDSON: When I finally
got put together,

00:02:04.600 --> 00:02:06.360
I went back expecting a big welcome.

00:02:06.520 --> 00:02:10.000
You know what they said?
You're history.

00:02:10.160 --> 00:02:13.040
Moved right on to the next rookie
standing in line.

00:02:15.040 --> 00:02:19.320
There was a lot left in me
I never got a chance to show.

00:02:35.440 --> 00:02:36.600
(DOOR CREAKING)

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.640
Hey, Stickers.

00:02:39.520 --> 00:02:40.520
Hey, Sal.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:42.560
How you feeling?

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.600
Yeah, great. (SIGHS)

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:47.760
Really, really great.

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:50.360
Been thinking about Doc again?

00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:51.520
(SIGHS)

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:56.520
Yeah. You know they told him
when he was done.

00:02:57.680 --> 00:02:58.920
He didn't decide.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.640
I don't want what happened to Doc
to happen to me.

00:03:04.160 --> 00:03:05.320
But that hasn't happened.

00:03:06.080 --> 00:03:08.440
No, but I can't go out on the track

00:03:08.520 --> 00:03:10.960
and do the same old thing. It won't work.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:13.240
Then change it up! Try something new.

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:17.000
-I don't know, Sally. I--
-Don't fear failure.

00:03:17.160 --> 00:03:19.080
Be afraid of not having the chance.

00:03:19.120 --> 00:03:21.600
You have the chance. Doc didn't.

00:03:22.000 --> 00:03:26.080
And you can either take it or you can
do what you been doing. Sitting.

00:03:26.280 --> 00:03:28.440
In here. For months.

00:03:28.520 --> 00:03:31.200
And by the way,
I love what you've done with the place.

00:03:31.360 --> 00:03:35.040
I mean the monster movie lighting
and the musky air freshener.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:38.440
Don't let anyone tell you
you're not working that primer because...

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:41.080
Wow, I have never found you
more attractive.

00:03:41.600 --> 00:03:44.280
And now that I've been in here
for a couple minutes, the stench...

00:03:44.440 --> 00:03:47.960
-I'm getting kind of used to it.
-Okay, Sal. I get it. I get it.

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:50.880
I miss you, Lightning.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.040
We all do.

00:03:54.440 --> 00:03:55.800
(SIGHS)

00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:59.120
Try something new, huh?

00:04:01.120 --> 00:04:02.520
Hey, did it work, Miss Sally?

00:04:02.680 --> 00:04:03.720
Did you set him straight

00:04:03.800 --> 00:04:05.960
with your lawyerly powers
of persuasion?

00:04:06.120 --> 00:04:07.840
Is he ready to start training?

00:04:07.960 --> 00:04:10.000
Well, Stinky-- Stickers?

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:11.840
(CHUCKLES)

00:04:11.920 --> 00:04:14.160
Yes, Mater, I am.

00:04:14.480 --> 00:04:15.800
Whoo-hoo!

00:04:16.240 --> 00:04:18.080
I decide when I'm done.

00:04:18.720 --> 00:04:20.200
I was hoping you'd say that.

00:04:20.280 --> 00:04:21.680
Okay, but I got an idea.

00:04:21.840 --> 00:04:23.840
And I'm gonna need to talk
to Rusty and Dusty, all right?

00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:25.640
Oh, I'll get them on the horn.

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.440
(CHUCKLES) Get it? On the horn?

00:04:27.480 --> 00:04:29.360
(HONKS AND LAUGHS)

00:04:29.440 --> 00:04:32.400
Oops. Hold on. Got to sneeze.
(GASPING)

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.680
Dadgum, I lost it.
Hey, I'll see you at Flo's.

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:41.520
(SNEEZES LOUDLY)

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:43.000
I found it.

00:04:43.160 --> 00:04:44.640
Hey, watch your step.

00:04:45.680 --> 00:04:47.320
RUSTY ON SPEAKERS:
What about the car from Everett?

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.360
Remember him?

00:04:48.520 --> 00:04:49.520
He was stuck in reverse!

00:04:49.680 --> 00:04:52.360
I said, you need a house
with a circular driveway!

00:04:52.440 --> 00:04:53.440
(BOTH LAUGHING)

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:55.680
You need to get your
rusty tails down here.

00:04:55.760 --> 00:04:57.840
I created a drink in your honor.

00:04:58.000 --> 00:05:00.840
Yeah! The Rust-eze Medicated
Bumper Bomb.

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:03.840
It goes down faster
than an elevator full of Winnebagos.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.880
-McQUEEN: Rusty and Dusty!
-Well, look who's here.

00:05:07.360 --> 00:05:09.480
Hey, there he is!
Good to see you, Lightning!

00:05:09.680 --> 00:05:12.480
Thanks, guys. Wow. You're all here.

00:05:12.720 --> 00:05:15.160
Sorry, buddy,
did you want this call to be private?

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:20.200
No, Mater. This is perfect. Listen,
thanks, everyone, for sticking by me.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:23.600
It took me a while to figure it out,
but I know now that it's time...

00:05:24.000 --> 00:05:25.640
for me to make some changes.

00:05:25.880 --> 00:05:27.720
Changes? What kind of changes?

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:30.400
It's futile to resist change, man.

00:05:30.600 --> 00:05:32.560
-You're right, Fillmore.
-Really?

00:05:32.720 --> 00:05:35.200
Which is why I have
an announcement to make.

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:38.200
I've thought long and hard about it.

00:05:38.280 --> 00:05:42.040
Done a lot of soul-searching
and considered all of the options.

00:05:42.560 --> 00:05:45.240
And I've finally decided...

00:05:46.560 --> 00:05:48.280
You do want to keep racing?

00:05:48.520 --> 00:05:50.720
Are you kidding?
Of course I want to keep racing!

00:05:50.920 --> 00:05:53.080
-Thank goodness!
-Glad to hear it. All right.

00:05:53.320 --> 00:05:54.440
(SIGHS) Man, for a second I--

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:57.000
Wait a minute.
I knew that the whole time.

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.640
Guys! I'm talking about making
this my best season yet!

00:05:59.720 --> 00:06:01.400
We were hoping you'd say that.

00:06:01.880 --> 00:06:03.800
The thing is, if I'm gonna be
faster than Storm,

00:06:03.880 --> 00:06:05.200
I need to train like him.

00:06:05.440 --> 00:06:06.600
BOTH: We're way ahead of you, buddy!

00:06:06.760 --> 00:06:09.440
Lightning, we want you on the road
first thing in the morning...

00:06:09.600 --> 00:06:12.240
so you can come out
and see the brand-new...

00:06:12.400 --> 00:06:14.880
BOTH: Rust-eze Racing Center!

00:06:15.040 --> 00:06:18.440
-It's wicked awesome.
-What? Rust-eze Racing Center?

00:06:18.680 --> 00:06:22.760
It's got all the fancy bells and whistles
that kids are training on these days.

00:06:22.960 --> 00:06:24.680
We'll send Macky boy all the directions.

00:06:24.760 --> 00:06:26.440
Now get moving, all right?

00:06:27.160 --> 00:06:29.000
Okay! Yes!

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:31.760
-Fancy new training center?
-That sounds nice!

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:34.120
Guido, come! We have to pack the tires!

00:06:34.280 --> 00:06:37.080
Hey, McQueen!
You can't race in primer, man.

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.280
Come on! Let's go.

00:06:38.720 --> 00:06:39.960
(WHIRRING)

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:44.600
(CHUCKLES) Ramone,
you have done it again.

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:48.160
It's like the Sistine Chapel on wheels.

00:06:48.240 --> 00:06:50.960
-(ENGINE REVVING)
-I'm coming for you, Storm.

00:06:52.960 --> 00:06:55.640
SARGE: Morning, McQueen!
Hey, look at you.

00:06:55.800 --> 00:06:57.280
CAR 1: Oh!
CAR 2: He looks so good!

00:06:58.920 --> 00:07:01.840
Welcome back. You look different.

00:07:01.920 --> 00:07:04.680
-(CHUCKLES) Obviously.
-You look ready.

00:07:04.840 --> 00:07:07.320
Guido, come! Scusi, scusi.
Tires coming through.

00:07:07.480 --> 00:07:10.160
Go kick those rookies in the trunk.

00:07:10.320 --> 00:07:11.760
-(SALLY CHUCKLES)
-All right, bye.

00:07:11.960 --> 00:07:14.440
-Catch you on the flipside.
-I'll see you guys in Florida.

00:07:14.640 --> 00:07:16.880
-See you, McQueen.
-Don't forget to call me.

00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:19.160
-LIZZIE: Good luck in college.
-(CHUCKLES)

00:07:19.880 --> 00:07:22.400
Hey, Sal. Thanks.

00:07:22.760 --> 00:07:23.960
Anytime.

00:07:25.000 --> 00:07:27.120
-Love you!
-Love you more.

00:07:27.520 --> 00:07:30.000
Rust-eze Racing Center, here we come!

00:07:30.120 --> 00:07:31.520
-Good times ahead.
-(HORN BLOWING)

00:07:34.240 --> 00:07:35.880
(SOBBING)

00:07:38.160 --> 00:07:39.480
(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:41.680
♪ When the time gets right

00:07:43.160 --> 00:07:45.160
♪ I'm gonna pick you up

00:07:46.480 --> 00:07:48.760
♪ And take you far away from

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.080
♪ From trouble, my love

00:07:53.560 --> 00:07:55.520
♪ Under a big old sky

00:07:57.200 --> 00:07:59.280
♪ Out in a field of green

00:08:01.360 --> 00:08:03.680
♪ There's got to be something

00:08:04.680 --> 00:08:06.840
♪ Left for us to believe

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:11.160
♪ Oh, I await the day

00:08:11.760 --> 00:08:14.880
♪ Good fortune comes our way

00:08:15.200 --> 00:08:18.360
♪ And we'll ride down
the King's Highway

00:08:18.520 --> 00:08:21.880
♪ Yeah, yeah
Yeah ♪

